What this package redistributes
-------------------------------
The files under skills/ are the upstream skill bodies, copied verbatim from
https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman at commit
2e068f735253cce28256744804785f01887d9646 (upstream skill pack 2.2.0), with one
exception noted under "State changes": skills/caveman-compress/SKILL.md is adapted.
skills/native-core.md is upstream's skills/native/native-core.md, verbatim.

No code from upstream's CLI, proxy, engine, browse, MCP server, shrink, cavemem
or extension is redistributed here. The third-party attributions in the upstream
NOTICE (below) relate to that code, not to the skill texts.

State changes (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b))
-----------------------------------------------
- index.js (new file): registers the upstream skill bodies with the DeepSeek
  Harness skill registry and APPENDS a "DSH runtime" section to each body at load
  time. That note states host facts upstream assumes differently: DSH has no
  caveman hook, so the active mode is conversational and is not stored; status
  answers must be marked "(not tracked by this host)"; usage and savings are
  unmeasured on this host; DSH has no task classifier, so the native-pack skills
  are model-invocable rather than classifier-gated.
- skills/caveman-compress/SKILL.md (ADAPTED FILE, marked in its header): upstream
  ships a Python CLI that sends the file's text to the `claude` CLI, the Anthropic
  API or an OpenAI-compatible endpoint. This port removes the external endpoint and
  the Python script; the session's own model rewrites the file locally, the backup
  goes to .caveman/backups/ outside the source tree, and
  scripts/verify-compress.mjs gates the overwrite. The compression rules and the
  list of preserved constructs are upstream's.
- scripts/verify-compress.mjs (new file), test/, README.md, NOTICE, package.json,
  cordis.patch.yml, scripts/install-local.sh, scripts/uninstall-local.sh: new
  files for packaging, the local backup/gate workflow, the DSH bundle layer, tests
  and installation. No upstream code.
- Not ported: upstream's CLI, proxy, engine, MCP server and the skills that depend
  on them (cavecrew, caveman-discover, caveman-explore, caveman-learn,
  caveman-manage, caveman-optimize, caveman-setup, caveman-evidence-review). See
  the "caveman" field in package.json.

